    "body": "Adopt the published Builds 4.44.2 / Platform v1.3.0 tuple for blocking disposable package integration, using immutable Builds executor `ae68c59bd2f4145a23ccf68c3711f98eaf62195f` in ordinary CI and the registered lifecycle baseline. Preserve all 15 isolated projects, independent owner gates, incoming source selections, publication controls and existing budgets.\n\nEnable exact Memories 3.0.23 refresh and FrontComposer 4.7.6 UI/readiness capabilities in the owning finite selectors. Keep unknown-package fallbacks and strict served-asset identity checks. The native suite retains real Parties/Tenants/Memories persistence assertions, adds anonymous gateway 401 coverage and preserves bounded source/owner-bound SDK diagnostics.\n\nExclude only the generated root `/.hexalith/builds-execution/` checkout from caller Git status. The previous hosted attempt passed all 15 isolated projects (6,330 tests) and all six independent jobs, then the unchanged source-clean proof refused before provisioning. A real Git regression reproduces that generated-checkout dirtiness and verifies the exact exclusion while tracked source/test/declaration/config changes and unrelated or lookalike untracked paths remain visible.\n\nValidation: 449 affected .NET cases and 68 single-attempt local package browser cases passed for the capability correction. The generated-checkout correction passed five focused cases, an actual caller/Platform/Builds/helper layout check and signed 4.44.2 resource-free preparation; affected Release/package builds had zero warnings/errors. The hosted UI gate passed with one original configured retry; its first failure is retained.\n\nFresh complete hosted CI and the full trusted handoff/native execution with retained reports and exact cleanup remain required, followed by the three manual lifecycle scenarios. The new 401 fact has compiled and requires genuine hosted execution. Earlier failures remain preserved. No historical parity or candidate acceptance is claimed.\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Pins a new Platform/Builds tuple and expands native integration diagnostics and gateway authorization checks; product behavior is mostly compile-gating and test harness, but hosted CI and real-service lanes must still prove the adoption.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Adopts the **Story 2.8** released **Platform v1.3.0** and **Builds v4.44.2** tuple across the module CLI (`4.44.2`), reusable **domain-ci-v2** pins in ordinary and lifecycle CI, docs, README prerequisites, and **`.gitlink-signoff.tsv`**, with the prerequisite matrix and fitness tests updated to treat that tuple as current while preserving dated history.\n> \n> The effective package graph moves to **FrontComposer 4.7.6** and **Memories 3.0.23** via **`Directory.Build.targets`** (shared UI/readiness and Memories refresh compile symbols) plus matching **Ci.Tests** theory coverage and e2e UI asset expectations.\n> \n> CI and qualification wiring adds shallow **direct-only** submodule init for the platform-declaration job, ignores **`/.hexalith/builds-execution/`**, documents native SDK diagnostics after real persistence checks, and introduces **platform integration** hooks: bounded loaded/copied assembly observations bound to the G4 handoff, a live **anonymous command-status \u2192 401** gateway test, and caller-artifact / generated-checkout boundary tests.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit c83fead177ca91f4d4b5aa09fc2ec5826ae0f173. Bugbot is set up for automated code reviews on this repo. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->",
